# SRG-APP-000297-AU-000570  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must display an explicit logout message to users
# indicating the reliable termination of authenticated communications
# sessions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000297-AU-000570
group:           V-221924
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-002364
control_rev5:    AC-12

contribution:    Splunk Web renders its own logout page after a user-initiated logout; the
                 application displays the message but exposes no setting that supplies,
                 suppresses or alters its text.

external:        The wording of Splunk Web's built-in logout page is compiled into the
                 product, so an assessor confirms the explicit logout message by observing
                 a logout in the interface.
external:        Where logout redirects to a SAML identity provider or to a URL named by
                 redirectAfterLogoutToUrl, the final page the user sees is that service's
                 and is outside the application.
external:        Where the logout message must carry organization-specific wording, that is
                 a product feature request, not a configuration item.

manual_reason:   The wording of Splunk Web's logout page is compiled into the product and
                 no .conf setting in the 10.4.2 specification set expresses it, so the
                 explicit logout message is confirmed by observing a logout rather than by
                 reading a value.

citation:        The reviewed criterion contradicts itself: its own contribution text
                 states the logout page wording is compiled into the product and not
                 exposed by configuration, then makes the verdict turn on
                 authentication.conf redirectAfterLogoutToUrl. That setting has no default
                 and lives inside a SAML [<saml-authSettings-key>] stanza
                 (authentication.conf.spec:780-784) that exists only where authType is SAML
                 against a default of Splunk (authentication.conf.spec:30-33), so as the
                 single ANDed condition it reports a finding on every instance not using
                 SAML - a finding for a message the product displays and no setting can
                 change. The messages.conf keys the inventory carries for this requirement
                 do not reach it either: [<component>:<key>] message, action and target
                 define platform bulletin messages keyed to a component the software itself
                 raises, with target choosing between Splunk Web and the log
                 (messages.conf.spec:68-73, 79-83, 116-124), and there is no component or
                 key for a user-initiated logout. Nothing in the specification set
                 expresses the logout message, so the criterion is manual and
                 redirectAfterLogoutToUrl is recorded as the related SAML behavior, not as
                 a test.
finding:         Not expected to be a finding against the application: Splunk Web displays
                 its built-in logout page on a user-initiated logout, and an assessor
                 records that observation; raise a finding only if no logout confirmation
                 is displayed.
